{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_rkfitquzsa57ppkvi6wgb65gbpc2po3ye6lrsledxcz7eu3cuibq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases done, with every gate independently re-checked on disk.\n\n## What I did\n\n**Setup.** `cargo check` was already clean (no compile errors). Built the C reference via cmake (`c_src/build/libharvest-work-6VP3Pl.so` — the name comes from the workdir, so the tests glob `*.so`), added `libloading` to `[dev-dependencies]` (the sandbox has no crates.io access, so everything runs `--offline` against the local cache; `Cargo.lock` is now complete so plain `cargo test` works too).\n\n**Phase A** — three artifacts derived mechanically from the C:\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — 22 exported symbols, **0 missing** in the Rust `.so`, 0 non-libc undefined. `src/lib.c` is the whole library, so nothing was left untranslated.\n- `ERRORS.md` — **35 rows**, one per distinct rejection: each `return 0` branch, all four `d0..d3` separating-axis flags of both AABB predicates, the NaN paths, `out == NULL`, div-by-±0, the `switch` with no `default`.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — **40 rows** over 13 axes (dispatch mode, entry level, all 10 capsule sub-paths, all 4 AABB axis winners, box/ray/radius shapes, float classes, `out` pre-state).\n\n**Phases B/C** — 79 tests in `tests/`, all loading **both** `.so`s via `libloading` (no direct Rust calls). Branch coverage is *proved*, not assumed: `tests/common/mod.rs` classifies each call's sub-path by recomputing the branch conditions **through the C library's own exports**, and each row asserts its intended sub-path was reached. Final pass: **62,929,792 bit comparisons, 0 mismatches**.\n\n**Phase D** — `./verify.sh` runs the whole matrix (2 feature combos × dev/release cdylib × C `-O0`/`-O2` × 4 suites) plus a symbol diff per build: **ALL CHECKS PASSED**.\n\n## Three C behaviours that can't be byte-matched — pinned down rather than glossed over\n\n1. **NaN payloads** (two NaN operands into one `mulss`/`addss`): the C `-O0` and `-O2` builds of the *same source* differ on **2210** payloads, while Rust differs from the reference on **1676** — the C has no single behaviour here. Non-NaN results are compared bit-exactly always; `tests/nan_payload_policy.rs` asserts Rust is never worse than another C build (`SPEC_RAY_STRICT_NAN=1` to inspect).\n2. **`c2CastRay` with an out-of-range enum**: the `switch` has no `default`, so it falls off the end without writing `eax`. I measured **5 different \"return values\" in 5 separate processes** (ASLR). Rust returns a deterministic 0; the tests assert the entire *defined* contract instead (`*out` untouched for 15 invalid values, no crash, later valid calls unaffected).\n3. **Null-pointer faults**: the release cdylib SIGSEGVs identically to the C (verified in child processes); the dev cdylib aborts instead because `debug-assertions` catches the null deref itself. The tests accept exactly those two forms.\n\nI did not modify anything under `c_src/` (source md5s and timestamps unchanged; only the sanctioned `build/` directory was added). The one fix I made and then reverted was a NaN-payload operand-order tweak in `src/lib.rs` — LLVM canonicalizes commutative operands, so it changed nothing, and the C's own self-disagreement showed there was no target to hit; the translation now mirrors the C source literally. `VERIFICATION.md` records the full report."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":894,"cache_read_input_tokens":293599,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":894,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a64656e4-9028-40a9-a432-74e58c4815ab","uuid":"33ae4fcc-d3be-4597-b395-94ea31732390","timestamp":"2026-08-27T17:45:31.287Z"}
